    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d283">

                <pb facs="0530" n="493" xml:id="pg493"/>

                <head>283. Telegram From the Mission to the United
                        Nations to the Department of State<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d283-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>New York</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1969-11-12T01:03:00+00:00">November 12, 1969,
                        0103Z</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>4146. Chirep Vote Results.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>
                        UNGA voted Nov 11 on Chirep reses with following results: <list>
                            <label>A.</label>
                            <item>Important Question res adopted by
                                vote of 71–48–4, 3 absent (73–47–5 in 1968).</item>
                            <label>B.</label>
                            <item>Albanian res defeated 48–56–21, 1
                                absent (44–58–23 in 1968). (This one vote less than margin forecast
                                    USUN 3978.)<anchor n="2"
                                    xml:id="d283-f2"/>
                            </item>
                        </list>
                    </item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Changes from 1968 were as follows: <list>
                            <label>A.</label>
                            <item>Important Question: Ecuador–Abstain to yes; Equatorial Guinea–Yes
                                to absent; Kuwait–No to absent; Libya–yes to no; Malaysia–Yes to
                                abstain; Morocco–No to abstain. Favorable margin thus decreased from
                                26 to 23.</item>
                            <label>B.</label>
                            <item>Albanian res: No to abstain: Belgium, Chile and Italy; Abstain to
                                yes: Ghana, Libya, Mauritius and Nigeria. Only favorable change was
                                Senegal from abstain to no. Favorable margin thus decreased from 14
                                to 8.</item>
                        </list>
                    </item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#bold">Yost</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
